import lib/process.dl

set argument to a new string buffer containing 3 bytes
store 65 as a byte into the data of argument at 0
store 0 as a byte into the data of argument at 1
store 66 as a byte into the data of argument at 2

set command to a process command for "unused-executable"
add argument as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it
set expected to the string form of "Process argument must not be null or contain a zero byte"

print lines (child failed to launch) and (the starting error of child = expected)

run command and set result to it
print lines (result failed to launch), (result failed) and (result's error message = expected)
